<title>USA: TABLE-Northstar Health Q2 loss widens.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Northstar Health Q2 loss widens.</headline>
<dateline>INDIANA, Pa. 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northstar Health Services Inc</p>
<p>	    3 Months</p>
<p>				1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr	 loss	    $0.57     loss	 $0.38</p>
<p> Net	 loss	    3,353     loss	 2,338</p>
<p> Revs			  8,032		   10,112</p>
<p> Avg shrs		    5,867		    6,229</p>
<p>	  6  MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr	loss	    $0.84     loss	 $0.76</p>
<p> Net	loss	    4,949     loss	 4,706</p>
<p> Revs			17,215		   20,962</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   5,867		    6,229</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Company says decline was the result of the transfer of contracts, pursuant to a separation agreement and the closure or termination of clinics and contracts, the majority of which were unprofitable.</p>
<p>Company says increase in net loss can be attributed to the neto operating losses related to the company's subacute care contracts in Illinois.  The contracts were terminated in July 1997.</p>
